2 CONTEXT IMMERSION
The following chapter presents the project’s starting point and the context it is carried out within. The section present insights from an earlier project on the subject, technological innovation within the automotive industry, an overview of the technologies used, and what similar products there are today.
2.1 PREVIOUS AR-HUD PROJECT
In fall 2021, at Lulea University of Technology, a similar project on creating visual information in an AR-HUD was carried out. The project aimed to design conceptual prototypes and evaluate them with users. A team of students2 did this project, seen as a pilot study. Prototypes and concepts in this project did not consider any technical limitations, which decreased the feasibility of the results and conclusions. These facts considered, insights and conclusions can still be helpful in this project.
The project’s helpful insights are that the amount of information is essential for users to perceive AR-HUD as a useful aid. Timing of graphics was concluded as a factor of a successful implementation and affordance of the graphics design. Colors were also tested, which gave insights into color usage in AR-HUD. The pilot project showed it was difficult to interview users regarding AR-HUD technology because it is new and unavailable to the public. It was difficult for users to express or define needs being unfamiliar with the technology.
2.2 THE AUTOMOTIVE INDUSTRY
One of the most prominent industries in Europe is the automotive industry (Casper & Sundin, 2021), and the sales of new cars in Europe in 2021 were 9,7 million vehicles (Acea, 2021). Being at the forefront of technological advancements is the goal of companies within many industries, and the automotive industry has always pioneered in taking advantage of advancements in technology (Boboc, Gîrbacia, & Butilă, 2020). AR caught the industry’s interest for its potential and accessibility to implement new and innovative solutions. Areas of advanced manufacturing, virtual prototyping, vehicle safety automation, and user-friendly interface design that improve user and driving experience are areas where the automotive industry has advanced over the recent years with the implementation of AR (Boboc, et al., 2020).
2.3 VOLVO CARS
As one of the stakeholders for this project, Volvo Cars have implemented HUD solutions projecting information on the driver’s windshield (Volvo Cars, 2020). Volvo’s HUDs display information on current speed, cruise control, navigation, road signs, and warning messages on a single virtual image plane projected at two meters in front of the driver (Volvo Cars, 2020).
2.4 AUGMENTED REALITY
The meaning of the word Augment is strengthened or amplified (NE, n.d.) which gives the meaning of Augmented Reality (AR) being strengthening- or amplifying reality.
2 Aly Bardan, Linnea Bergensten, Jenny Gräsvik, Johan Hansols & Simon Vicini.
