4.3 CONTEXT IMMERSION
To explore and describe the context and starting point of this project, and the context section of this thesis presents the research and information necessary to give the reader sufficient knowledge leading up to this project. Methods presented in this section were implemented in chapter 2.
4.3.1 COMPETITOR ANALYSIS Competitor analyses during design projects gain valuable insights when researching design development projects. Competitive design solutions show features, functions, and flows that design solutions in development must compete with (DaSilva, 2020). It is essential to consider how competitors create their solutions and could evolve solutions in the future to distinguish the projects solutions to theirs (Wikberg Nilsson, Ericson, & Törlind, 2015).
