APPENDIX A – Ideation workshop Plan 1/1

The plans for the ideation workshop. Defining exercises and time plan for the execution.

Ideation session/workshop
1. Start by giving a short introduction of the projects and workshops context.
2. Warm-up exercise: Flip Book (Johan Lindqvist method card) Introduction and creativity. Max 10 min. Explaining exercise. 30 sec for each page. Some time to present yourself. Questions: 1. Sketching, describe your hometown. 2. Sketching, describe your first job. 3. Describe your favorite travel destination in 5 words. (Without naming country) 4. In text, describe your favorite color. (Without naming it) 5. Describe what superpower you would like to have with a sketch. 6. Sketching, describe the title of your favorite song. 7. Sketch the weirdest/most unusual food you have eaten. 8. Name as many things you can do with a paperclip. 9. Sketch a description of your best personal characteristic.
Presentation of flip book.
3. Reversed brainstorming: ideas for graphics that would be bad to implement. How might we not design graphics that guide drivers in an AR-HUD? 3 min ideas, 5 min discussion/presentation.
4. Brainstorming: Ideas that solve the problem. How might we design guiding graphics in an AR-HUD? 3min x 5 Scenarios: turn, change Lane, keep/hold lane, and going into roundabout. Presentation and discussion when all scenarios are gone thru.

